   w3/w8/wb on the forward arm: (False, True, True); on the backward arm: (True, True, True)
   walks of the trichotomy serving both arms: ['w8', 'wb']
   walks of the four-leg family serving both arms: 15
  (witness-batch72-break.txt is absent)

The reading of the result: a running arm of a faithful pair, at a basepoint
of the branch (LowAt on both arms), can fail Valley3BeforeNine -- so the
statement is not a fact about a running arm of a faithful pair with the
branch hypothesis.  At every such failure the two arms share the walk w8,
so the basepoint is not a crossing; on the corpus no crossing fails.
